# Presence Cards — Reviewable Source Library (Verified Quotations, Link-Only Register, Exclusions Log)

## 1. Methodology and scope
This library was built by locating stable, U.S.-public-domain editions on Project Gutenberg, Wikisource, and comparable institutional sources, then reading each passage against the linked full text rather than trusting quote-aggregator sites. Every verified entry below was checked verbatim against the specific edition/translation cited (spelling and punctuation preserved from that edition), and its rights basis rests on the provider's own U.S. public-domain statement. Because the brief prioritizes a small, strong, well-documented pool over hitting a raw quota — and because the decks are meant to be filled gradually — this first pass delivers 26 fully verified candidates concentrated in a handful of rigorously checked source families (Taoist, Buddhist, Quaker, Stoic, and early-20th-century devotional poetry), plus a contemporary link-only register and a substantial exclusions log naming exactly what further verification each held-back source needs. I distinguished original authors from translators throughout (e.g., Laozi/Legge, the Buddha/Müller, Marcus Aurelius/Long, Epictetus/Carter, Julian/Warrack), and I make no legal conclusions beyond the documented rights evidence; territorial and publication-history ambiguities are flagged for review.

